<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  REFERENCE ONLY — DO NOT INSTALL THIS FILE.

  This is what scripts/gen-privapp-permissions.sh produced for one specific build:

      microG GmsCore 0.3.16.252432
      LineageOS 22.2 / Android 15 (SDK 35)

  It is included so you can see the expected shape and sanity-check your own output.
  Generate your own instead:

      ./scripts/gen-privapp-permissions.sh

  Using a list from a different microG build is unsafe. Under
  ro.control_privapp_permissions=enforce a missing entry means the permission is
  denied, and on userdebug builds it can stop the device from booting.

  The entry that makes network location possible is INSTALL_LOCATION_PROVIDER.
-->
